WEBVTT

00:01.930 --> 00:04.840
Winter had almost come to our island.

00:05.620 --> 00:08.700
Let your heart be silent and remember those tiny memories,

00:08.700 --> 00:10.670
and think back to what happened then.

00:11.240 --> 00:12.700
Ten years of days and nights...

00:13.580 --> 00:17.400
On this island, we grew up just a little.

00:17.400 --> 00:19.990
Um, who are you?

00:36.140 --> 00:41.260
Today I shout out another good morning courageously

00:41.260 --> 00:46.560
The sparkling chime of hope is resounding

00:47.050 --> 00:52.140
The gentle sun is always

00:52.140 --> 00:57.660
Blessing the late coming sensation of the two of them

00:57.950 --> 01:02.880
To fall in love with a goddess is the best!

01:03.090 --> 01:12.950
Even if she is a beatrice I can't control this throbbing feeling

01:12.950 --> 01:13.800
L·O·V·E

01:13.800 --> 01:15.550
I love you MA·MO·RU!

01:15.550 --> 01:17.090
These overflowing feelings

01:17.090 --> 01:19.790
Take them high into the sky

01:19.790 --> 01:24.680
Please grant me my dazzling and sparkling dream

01:24.680 --> 01:26.480
That's right MA·MO·RU!

01:26.480 --> 01:28.010
Only for you

01:28.010 --> 01:30.680
I will show you my power of miracles

01:30.680 --> 01:32.950
I will surely, surely swear

01:32.950 --> 01:38.900
I will not end my Shining Love

02:00.110 --> 02:02.650
Excuse me, can you help us over here?

02:02.650 --> 02:03.310
I’m coming!

02:18.590 --> 02:21.100
They told you, right?

02:21.100 --> 02:22.680
I’m going to believe.

02:22.680 --> 02:24.740
Because I know.

02:26.650 --> 02:28.420
Will you believe?

02:30.240 --> 02:30.910
Yeah!

02:30.910 --> 02:32.590
I will!

02:38.640 --> 02:39.480
I’m starting.

02:39.480 --> 02:40.300
Get back.

03:03.420 --> 03:05.070
Don’t worry.

03:05.070 --> 03:08.160
We, and you, will all be able to leave.

03:09.260 --> 03:10.380
Why?

03:10.380 --> 03:12.850
The power to create miracles...

03:12.850 --> 03:16.910
If I told you that, would you believe me?

03:27.490 --> 03:28.940
Ayako!

03:37.360 --> 03:42.430
In a Storm

03:56.570 --> 03:57.630
Mamoru...

03:57.630 --> 03:58.340
Mamoru!

04:02.320 --> 04:03.180
Ayako-san?

04:04.780 --> 04:06.020
I’m so relieved...

04:15.850 --> 04:18.730
Damn that hag!

04:37.430 --> 04:41.490
Even at times like these, you get hungry.

04:45.420 --> 04:46.480
You OK?

04:46.480 --> 04:47.670
You hurt?

04:47.670 --> 04:48.800
I’m fine.

04:49.340 --> 04:50.530
Ayako-san!

04:50.530 --> 04:52.220
Is your arm injured?

04:52.220 --> 04:53.390
It’s just a scratch.

04:53.390 --> 04:54.750
But your blood...

04:54.750 --> 04:55.990
It’s fine.

04:55.990 --> 04:59.570
Anyway, we need to get out of here.

05:02.960 --> 05:04.540
There’s no obvious exit.

05:04.980 --> 05:06.400
So...

05:06.400 --> 05:07.760
Ayako-san?

05:07.760 --> 05:10.350
We need to get to the Rainbow Cape.

05:37.980 --> 05:40.940
The beatrice is sealed away.

05:56.720 --> 05:58.420
U-Um...

05:58.420 --> 05:59.550
What?

05:59.550 --> 06:00.730
Em-chan?

06:00.730 --> 06:04.040
Wh-Where are Mamoru and Witch Beatrice?

06:04.040 --> 06:06.870
We can’t find them.

06:06.870 --> 06:09.140
Maybe... Maybe they...

06:09.500 --> 06:11.530
They’re spending the night outside!

06:11.530 --> 06:13.270
No!

06:13.710 --> 06:16.730
Oh, sweet memory!

06:16.730 --> 06:18.950
On a night like this?

06:18.950 --> 06:20.490
Don’t worry.

06:20.490 --> 06:22.250
Ayako is with him.

06:22.250 --> 06:25.000
This storm is nothing.

06:25.000 --> 06:26.990
Oh, Brother!

06:27.540 --> 06:29.560
That’s right.

06:29.560 --> 06:32.700
Witch Beatrice is with him.

06:43.560 --> 06:46.010
The beatrice is sealed?

06:46.010 --> 06:47.970
Who did it?

06:51.260 --> 06:52.470
That’s crazy!

06:52.780 --> 06:54.320
Stop it, Ayako-san!

07:00.640 --> 07:02.370
Ayako-san?

07:02.370 --> 07:03.910
Are you OK?

07:03.910 --> 07:05.460
This is pathetic...

07:06.010 --> 07:12.180
I’m here with you, and I can’t protect you...

07:13.180 --> 07:14.500
Ayako-san...

07:15.570 --> 07:17.830
You protected me back there.

07:23.760 --> 07:26.750
You’ll waste energy if you move around.

07:27.130 --> 07:28.520
Don’t worry.

07:28.520 --> 07:31.720
The President and the others will
notice and come for us.

07:33.010 --> 07:34.100
Thank you.

07:34.590 --> 07:37.340
Let’s do our best until then.

07:37.340 --> 07:41.890
That earthquake... I wonder if Mary-chan is OK.

07:42.740 --> 07:43.940
<i>It’s raining!</i>

07:43.940 --> 07:47.050
<i>No, I stopped it with beatrice!</i>

07:47.050 --> 07:48.780
<i>Let’s hurry, Ayako-san.</i>

07:48.780 --> 07:49.740
<i>Be careful!</i>

07:50.220 --> 07:52.020
<i>Bye!</i>

07:53.570 --> 07:56.260
<i>It can’t be... She lured us here?</i>

07:56.720 --> 07:58.620
<i>But why?</i>

07:58.620 --> 08:04.340
If she’s safe, she’ll let the rest of
the student council know.

08:18.530 --> 08:19.470
Who’s that?

08:24.600 --> 08:25.980
Takasu Masaki?

08:27.400 --> 08:29.160
Masaki-san...

08:29.160 --> 08:29.710
No way...

08:29.710 --> 08:32.410
Maya, Shione, follow me!

08:32.410 --> 08:34.990
Masaki-san, what’s wrong?

08:34.990 --> 08:36.900
What are you doing here?

08:36.900 --> 08:38.390
We’ll talk later.

08:38.390 --> 08:40.690
Ayako and that boy are in danger!

08:40.690 --> 08:41.840
Ayako?

08:42.410 --> 08:45.120
She’s up against the Silver Maria.

08:45.750 --> 08:47.630
The Silver Maria?

09:01.080 --> 09:03.190
<i>The power to create miracles...</i>

09:03.890 --> 09:06.650
<i>If I told you that, would you believe me?</i>

09:11.000 --> 09:14.430
The Silver Maria, a beatrice user on par

09:14.430 --> 09:17.060
with Johan and Ayako, one of the best in the world.

09:17.060 --> 09:21.410
But her power surpasses theirs.

09:21.410 --> 09:25.230
She’s after Ayako-san and Mamoru-san?

09:25.230 --> 09:26.780
That’s awful.

09:26.780 --> 09:28.040
It’s awful!

09:29.790 --> 09:30.830
It’s useless.

09:30.830 --> 09:31.460
Watch.

09:33.810 --> 09:34.720
This is...

09:35.020 --> 09:36.340
A Horacle.

09:36.340 --> 09:37.230
A Horacle?

09:37.730 --> 09:40.580
It’s a device that stops beatrice from working.

09:41.480 --> 09:43.770
They’re scattered all over the forest.

09:44.520 --> 09:47.120
You can’t use beatrice here.

09:47.120 --> 09:49.150
Which includes Ayako.

09:49.540 --> 09:51.620
Then what will happen to them?

09:51.620 --> 09:54.970
If they can’t use beatrice, even Ayako...

09:54.970 --> 09:57.580
Ayako has to be safe.

09:57.580 --> 10:00.210
She’s practically a monster herself,

10:00.210 --> 10:04.840
and her beloved Mamoru’s with her...
She wouldn’t die here.

10:04.840 --> 10:05.850
I’m sorry.

10:05.850 --> 10:08.480
What do we do?

10:08.480 --> 10:11.020
We have to destroy these things

10:11.020 --> 10:15.890
until their power weakens and we can use beatrice again.

10:15.890 --> 10:17.340
One by one...

10:17.340 --> 10:19.100
How many are there?

10:19.100 --> 10:21.370
I don’t know. Probably very many...

10:21.880 --> 10:22.990
Emelenzia-san!

10:27.100 --> 10:28.490
I’ll find them.

10:28.490 --> 10:30.090
I’ll find them all!

10:30.090 --> 10:32.400
I have to! I have to do it!

10:35.090 --> 10:37.840
Let’s get started, too!

10:38.940 --> 10:40.360
Yeah!

10:42.580 --> 10:45.540
<i>Wait for me, Mamoru!</i>

10:50.920 --> 10:53.150
Come on, Horacle!

10:53.150 --> 10:55.900
Horacle, Horacle, wake up!

10:56.770 --> 10:58.340
Found one!

11:00.820 --> 11:02.370
I found one!

11:01.730 --> 11:02.370
Here, too!

11:03.310 --> 11:04.640
Found ya!

11:05.450 --> 11:06.100
Here’s one!

11:06.100 --> 11:07.310
Crush!

11:09.370 --> 11:10.530
Not yet.

11:10.530 --> 11:11.480
It’s still weak.

11:11.480 --> 11:12.860
I can’t find them.

11:12.860 --> 11:14.080
I can’t...

11:14.080 --> 11:15.690
I can’t find any...

11:16.080 --> 11:17.110
I found one!

11:27.090 --> 11:28.480
Ayako-san.

11:28.480 --> 11:31.060
It’s a bit better like this, isn’t it?

11:32.080 --> 11:33.460
Ayako-san...

11:45.280 --> 11:46.310
Why is it, I wonder.

11:47.140 --> 11:51.550
When I’m with you, I feel like everything will be OK.

11:51.550 --> 11:53.020
Me, too.

11:53.020 --> 11:56.520
Actually, I was in an accident like this long ago.

11:57.440 --> 12:00.230
I told you once, right?

12:00.760 --> 12:04.180
About why I was so interested in beatrice.

12:04.690 --> 12:08.510
I was in an accident when I was little.

12:08.510 --> 12:12.270
And a man who used beatrice saved me.

12:13.660 --> 12:15.220
It was when I was seven.

12:15.760 --> 12:18.710
I was going to my grandfather’s house in the country, alone.

12:18.710 --> 12:19.780
And on the way...

12:30.140 --> 12:31.170
<i>Hey, kid.</i>

12:31.850 --> 12:33.610
<i>Don’t worry.</i>

12:33.610 --> 12:36.650
<i>We, and you, will all be able to leave.</i>

12:36.650 --> 12:37.610
<i>Why?</i>

12:38.640 --> 12:41.400
<i>The power to create miracles...</i>

12:41.400 --> 12:44.740
<i>If I told you that, would you believe me?</i>

12:45.850 --> 12:50.190
There was a girl with him then...

12:50.190 --> 12:53.000
My age or a bit older.

12:53.000 --> 12:56.790
She held my hand like this.

12:57.600 --> 12:59.570
She told me it would be all right.

12:59.570 --> 13:02.490
It wasn’t just because of the man,
but because of that girl, too,

13:03.050 --> 13:07.490
that I was able to have courage.

13:13.160 --> 13:15.340
Mamoru, you...

13:31.800 --> 13:33.880
Still not enough, Masaki-san?

13:35.000 --> 13:37.260
I can’t find them anywhere.

13:37.890 --> 13:40.310
It looks like we’ve cleared out this area.

13:40.310 --> 13:41.420
All that’s left is...

13:46.590 --> 13:47.900
You can’t mean...

13:49.820 --> 13:50.870
But...

13:51.850 --> 13:53.430
Emelenzia!

13:55.450 --> 13:56.510
Mamoru...

13:59.810 --> 14:01.650
<i>Hello.</i>

14:04.670 --> 14:06.020
E-Emelenzia!

14:06.020 --> 14:06.770
That’s dangerous!

14:06.770 --> 14:07.900
Don’t even try it!

14:07.900 --> 14:09.350
Anna, get the President!

14:09.350 --> 14:09.950
Right!

14:11.110 --> 14:12.210
Emelenzia!

14:15.000 --> 14:16.630
<i>Mamoru!</i>

14:16.630 --> 14:18.540
<i>Th-That’s right...</i>

14:18.540 --> 14:20.540
<i>Why are you here, anyway?</i>

14:22.770 --> 14:23.910
<i>Really?!</i>

14:23.910 --> 14:25.550
<i>Thank you!</i>

14:25.550 --> 14:27.010
Great!

14:27.480 --> 14:28.780
Emelenzia!

14:30.840 --> 14:32.390
<i>Mamoru...</i>

14:38.850 --> 14:40.090
<i>Wonderful!</i>

14:40.090 --> 14:40.950
<i>Great!</i>

14:40.950 --> 14:42.860
<i>You need to relax.</i>

14:43.710 --> 14:44.920
<i>H-Hey...</i>

14:50.460 --> 14:52.620
Um, Emelenzia...

14:54.080 --> 14:54.990
<i>Mamoru...</i>

14:56.170 --> 14:58.040
Maya, over there!

15:11.940 --> 15:13.720
I’d like to try it, too.

15:15.100 --> 15:15.930
<i>Mamoru...</i>

15:16.250 --> 15:17.890
<i>It’s still a bit cold, OK?</i>

15:19.100 --> 15:20.060
See you!

15:20.440 --> 15:21.190
<i>Mamoru...</i>

15:21.790 --> 15:23.190
<i>I can’t accept that.</i>

15:23.190 --> 15:24.770
<i>I can’t!</i>

15:25.820 --> 15:26.870
<i>Mamoru...</i>

15:30.700 --> 15:32.320
What should we do?

15:32.760 --> 15:33.910
<i>Mamoru!</i>

15:55.510 --> 15:56.560
Ayako-san?

15:59.250 --> 16:01.370
The beatrice is coming back.

16:01.830 --> 16:02.660
Masaki-san!

16:02.660 --> 16:04.240
No, it’s still weak.

16:11.360 --> 16:13.280
I may be able to do it.

16:13.280 --> 16:14.180
Ayako-san...

16:14.180 --> 16:15.740
It’s OK. Leave it to me.

16:23.020 --> 16:25.280
Do you believe?

16:28.680 --> 16:29.950
Ayako-san.

16:29.950 --> 16:31.850
You’re not ready yet.

16:31.850 --> 16:33.340
You believe, right?

16:35.710 --> 16:38.210
The power to create miracles...

16:38.210 --> 16:42.410
If I told you that, would you believe me?

16:45.600 --> 16:47.840
Yes! I believe you!

16:58.260 --> 17:00.540
This is Ayako?

17:03.080 --> 17:05.370
Mamoru... It’s Mamoru!

17:49.020 --> 17:50.010
Ayako-san!

17:50.010 --> 17:50.920
I’m amazed.

17:52.590 --> 17:55.200
To do all this with the beatrice incomplete...

17:55.200 --> 17:59.980
You’ve grown up, Ayako.

18:05.880 --> 18:07.520
Masaki... Why?

18:21.140 --> 18:23.310
The Silver Maria invented this.

18:23.310 --> 18:26.630
But this is incomplete.

18:26.630 --> 18:28.530
If it were the real thing, you would...

18:28.530 --> 18:30.780
But why would the Silver Maria...

18:30.780 --> 18:32.330
Who knows?

18:32.330 --> 18:34.980
The world is filled with mysteries and contradictions.

18:34.980 --> 18:37.170
So what are you doing here?

18:38.220 --> 18:40.340
I came to see your boyfriend.

18:43.590 --> 18:44.180
Masaki!

18:44.180 --> 18:45.370
Well?

18:45.370 --> 18:49.670
Can you believe in the power to create miracles now?

18:51.050 --> 18:52.050
Yes.

18:53.680 --> 18:55.250
You’re a good man.

18:58.920 --> 19:00.910
Are you going to stay with him?

19:05.720 --> 19:07.720
It’s not just the world.

19:07.720 --> 19:10.790
There are mysteries and contradictions in me, as well.

19:16.860 --> 19:18.860
Morning, Mr. Tsune ...

19:20.530 --> 19:26.190
You’re calling me Mr. Tsune... Who are you?

19:28.750 --> 19:30.600
Hey there, Mr. Tsune.

19:33.350 --> 19:38.450
I-I had no idea you were here...
You should’ve said something.

19:38.450 --> 19:39.390
No!

19:39.390 --> 19:42.880
If you’re here about my work, it’s been perfect.

19:42.880 --> 19:47.020
I haven’t taken my eyes off Ayako-san...
I mean, Takasu Ayako.

19:47.020 --> 19:48.550
Really?

19:48.550 --> 19:49.720
Really!

19:51.150 --> 19:52.860
I’m serious!

19:52.860 --> 19:54.070
Right, right.

19:54.070 --> 19:54.710
I get it.

19:55.340 --> 19:57.470
I got the data I needed.

19:57.470 --> 19:59.640
Next time is for real, Witch Beatrice.

20:00.510 --> 20:05.840
You’ll be busy when you get back to Japan, Mr. Tsune.

20:05.840 --> 20:06.830
Yes!

20:06.830 --> 20:08.370
With pleasure!

20:08.370 --> 20:10.060
Liar.

20:10.060 --> 20:12.350
Look at my eyes!

20:12.350 --> 20:14.110
Are these the eyes of a liar—

20:14.650 --> 20:18.320
Don’t take your glasses off!

20:19.700 --> 20:23.490
Maria... Silver Maria...

20:24.840 --> 20:28.260
I remember that boy, also.

20:28.880 --> 20:31.360
Actually, I was scared, too.

20:31.360 --> 20:36.280
But then I realized
that I was being cheered up.

20:37.300 --> 20:40.510
That boy’s smile saved me.

20:40.510 --> 20:44.000
That was you then, Mamoru.

20:44.000 --> 20:47.850
That was you then, Ayako-san...

20:48.330 --> 20:52.990
Back then, I never would have believed in eternal love.

20:53.840 --> 20:55.800
But now...

20:56.380 --> 20:57.530
Ayako-san...

21:05.420 --> 21:07.560
She even brought out the Horacles.

21:07.560 --> 21:10.100
Looks like she’s serious.

21:12.110 --> 21:12.870
Yeah.

21:12.870 --> 21:14.750
She’ll act again. I’m sure of it.

21:15.990 --> 21:18.970
Oh, and I met Yoshimura Mamoru.

21:20.080 --> 21:25.140
Yeah, he was just as you said, Johan.

21:25.140 --> 21:27.390
Very interesting.

21:34.620 --> 21:36.070
<i>I understand.</i>

21:36.850 --> 21:38.890
<i>I understand now.</i>

21:40.520 --> 21:42.040
<i>I...</i>

22:01.290 --> 22:06.970
My heart is racing and I'm going to give you

22:06.970 --> 22:12.170
This sparkling emotion

22:12.560 --> 22:18.300
The evening color is dyed into this orange shirt

22:18.360 --> 22:23.450
I catch it from behind you and my heart throbbing

22:23.560 --> 22:30.410
It's an everyday thrill just to be with you

22:30.410 --> 22:37.840
I can't say it well enough but thank you

22:37.840 --> 22:43.040
Venus Dream the hidden power

22:43.040 --> 22:49.240
This feeling will change into that power

22:49.240 --> 22:54.360
Power Dream I found what I want to protect

22:54.360 --> 23:00.770
That is your smile and your feelings

23:15.320 --> 23:18.140
I love winter!

23:18.140 --> 23:20.550
The sound of crackling sticks in the fire...

23:20.550 --> 23:22.810
You can’t enjoy the flowers,

23:22.810 --> 23:25.490
but the falling leaves are romantic...

23:25.490 --> 23:27.170
And getting plain taiyaki and

23:27.170 --> 23:29.260
eating it right away, without the teachers finding me...

23:29.260 --> 23:30.830
It’s wonderful.

23:30.830 --> 23:33.110
Enjoy winter!

23:33.110 --> 23:35.080
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself.

23:35.080 --> 23:39.760
I’m female student A. I was looking
through the window in episode 1.

23:39.760 --> 23:43.210
Next time: Sparks Fly on Valentine’s.

23:39.760 --> 23:43.980
Sparks Fly on Valentine’s
